  "notes": "{差|さ}し{出|だ}す is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) formed from {差|さ}す (to hold up) + {出|だ}す (to put out). It suggests a polite or formal gesture of offering.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{差|さ}し{出|だ}している indicates the ongoing action of holding something out.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [thing]を{差|さ}し{出|だ}す — to hold out/present [thing]\n- [person]に[thing]を{差|さ}し{出|だ}す — to present [thing] to [person]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {手|て}を{差|さ}し{出|だ}す (hold out one's hand)\n- {名刺|めいし}を{差|さ}し{出|だ}す (present a business card)\n- {手紙|てがみ}を{差|さ}し{出|だ}す (send a letter)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {差出人|さしだしにん}: sender (of mail)\n- {差|さ}し{入|い}れ: gift brought when visiting\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出|だ}す: to take out (neutral)\n- {提出|ていしゅつ}する: to submit (formal documents)",
